WEBVTT

NOTE Hit Your Mark introduction. English captions.

1
00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:03.185
Three. Two. One. Hit your mark.

2
00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:07.874
On stage, a performer walks
toward a tape mark on the floor.

3
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.749
Every second, the distance
to the mark shrinks.

4
00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:16.392
In the pool, a swimmer pushes
off the wall and glides.

5
00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.781
Every second, the distance swum grows.

6
00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.560
One number goes down. One goes up.

7
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:24.656
But both of them are lines.

8
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:28.272
The slope is the rate: how
much it changes each second.

9
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:32.666
The intercept is the start: where
you are when the clock begins.

10
00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:36.111
Change either one, and
the whole line moves.

11
00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:37.955
Now here's the problem.

12
00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.408
The director moves the cue earlier.

13
00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.464
The coach wants a faster split.

14
00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:45.031
Keep the old plan, and you miss.

15
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:47.982
Early is wrong. Late is wrong.

16
00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:51.825
So what do you change:
the rate, or the start?

17
00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:57.350
Choose your scene. Build the model.
Graph it, adjust it, and hit your mark.
